      "description": "Distress is the experience of being pressed hard by circumstances — the inner state of the person who is genuinely struggling, caught in difficulty, under pressure from multiple directions. The Hebrew and Greek vocabulary is extensive and varied, covering physical suffering, emotional anguish, social crisis, and spiritual desolation. What marks distress is not merely that things are difficult but that the difficulty is acute enough to require help from outside oneself. The psalms are full of distress cries — and of the God who hears them.",
